  "visualBrief": "Complete principal Catherine Palace exterior: long blue/white/gold baroque body, returned north and south wings, three raised hall roofs and five projecting crowns, recessed multi-story windows, paired white pilasters, original simplified gilded trim, roof balustrades, supported main forecourt entry and five-domed palace chapel. Detached curved low forecourt ranges, Lyceum/connecting arch, Cameron gallery, garden pavilions and park stay native context. No interiors or copied statues,heraldry or inscriptions.",
